1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:08,967
Then the tightness starts. Old dust on
the stairs. Fear. My chest closes like
a fist, and my inhaler is empty. The
last puff went at the exchange.

2
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:14,767
Rule three. Fix your own lungs first.
Nobody finds anybody while he can't
breathe.

3
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:23,600
The clinic is one street over, and the
door is open. On the top shelf, a
spare inhaler, and a note in Dad's
handwriting. For him. Always keep one.

4
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:32,267
Two puffs. Out for four. In for two.
The tightness lets go, one finger at a
time. I don't know where my father is.
He still looked after me.
